WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:06.710
On August 9, 2018 a fighter jet dropped a
bomb on this street in Dahyan, Yemen.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.110
It exploded here, near a busy marketplace.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.869
Killing 40 children on a school bus.

00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:15.539
The plane was from a coalition led by Saudi
Arabia.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:21.360
They have conducted thousands of airstrikes
in Yemen since 2015 - many aimed at civilian targets.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.060
This is the bomb.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:29.349
And this photo, reportedly taken after the
attack, shows that the serial number - 94271

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:33.920
- corresponds to a 500-pound laser-guided
bomb built by the Lockheed Martin corporation.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.520
It was made in the United States.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.060
In fact, most of Saudi Arabia’s weapons
are.

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:45.190
The US is the biggest arms dealer in the world
- and Saudi Arabia is its number one customer.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.129
For nearly 75 years, the two countries
have been strategic allies — trying to keep

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:52.910
the Middle East stable for their own benefit.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.670
But today, the Middle East has fallen apart.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.170
And Saudi Arabia has been using US weapons
to make it worse.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.260
So why does the US sell Saudi Arabia so many
weapons…

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:03.920
and will it ever stop?

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:20.320
In 1938, a lot of it was discovered in the
new country of Saudi Arabia.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.180
"For here are more proved and readily accessible reserves

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.000
than in all of North and South America together."

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:33.440
In 1945, US President Franklin Roosevelt made
a deal with the Saudi King AbdulAziz al-Saud:

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:38.061
The Saudis would provide the US with a safe,
reliable source of oil and in exchange, the

00:01:38.061 --> 00:01:39.980
US would support and protect the Saudis.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.460
This was at a time when the US was making
other alliances in the Middle East.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:51.680
"Oil, however. Together with its strategic location, it has made this area important in world affairs."

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.460
But at first, US arms sales to their allies in the Middle
East were limited.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.180
The US hoped fewer weapons

00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:00.360
would mean less conflict and therefore a steady
supply of oil.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.240
But that didn't last for long.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.810
War broke out between Israel and these Arab
States.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.250
in 1967.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.879
This put the US in an awkward situation - it
had allies on both sides.

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:19.420
The US ultimately decided to sell fighter
jets to Israel to give them an advantage over

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.500
the Arab states.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.980
But war broke out again six years later.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.180
This time, the US sent thousands of tons of
arms to Israel .

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.940
This outraged the Arab allies, including Saudi
Arabia.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:32.950
So they struck back.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:38.380
"The oil producing countries of the Arab world decided to use their oil as a political weapon."

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.540
These Arab states cut-off oil supplies to
the US to protest their support of Israel...

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.480
And it caused a crisis.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.200
The price of oil nearly quadrupled in the
US.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.800
The cut-off ended several months later when
the US brokered a peace deal between Israel and Egypt.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:59.040
But to help rebuild its relationship with
its Arab allies, the US decided to sell

00:02:59.040 --> 00:02:59.860
them weapons.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.560
And the Saudis were particularly eager to buy.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:09.040
By the 1970s, oil profits had made Saudi Arabia’s
monarchy extraordinarily rich - and they could

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.080
afford to buy a range of advanced weapons.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.920
Between 1970 and '76, US sales to Saudi Arabia
skyrocketed.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.079
In the meantime just
across the Gulf, Iran had emerged as

00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:22.980
another extremely strategic ally to the US.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:25.750
Like Saudi Arabia, it was a large, oil-rich
country.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:30.469
But more importantly, it shared this long
border with the Soviet Union - America’s

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:32.460
primary enemy during the Cold War.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.980
So, President Nixon said the US would ““sell
Iran virtually any conventional weapons it

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:38.980
wanted.”

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.859
Together, Saudi Arabia and Iran became America’s
Twin Pillars in the Middle East.

00:03:45.859 --> 00:03:50.959
For the US, selling them guns, bombs, planes,
and tanks was a way to prevent the Soviets

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.700
from entering the Middle East, and protect the oil supply.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.299
And having these countries rely on American
weapons gave the US important leverage to

00:03:58.299 --> 00:04:00.680
dictate how and when they were used.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:04.370
It was also an important sign of trust and
support between allies.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:09.319
US arms came with years of training and maintenance,
so each weapons deal with Saudi Arabia, for

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.460
example, was a long-term commitment to work
together.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:17.880
This would prove to be important because Saudi
Arabia and the US would soon have to rely

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.380
even more on each other…

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.510
In 1979, the Islamic revolution overthrew
the pro-US Shah of Iran who was replaced by

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.910
a religious leader; Ayatollah Khomeini.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.080
Suddenly, one of the America’s twin pillars
turned on it.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.680
The new Iran was ambitious and extremely anti-American.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.780
While armed with $9B worth of American-made

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:38.780
weapons.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.570
And it was also the enemy of Saudi Arabia.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.320
Each saw itself as the leader of the muslim
world; and started competing for influence

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.090
in the Middle East.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:51.300
So Saudi Arabia continued to want more weapons and the US continued to sell them.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:58.070
In the meantime, the Soviet Union, which had
been developing its own alliances in the Middle East

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:02.780
for decades, started selling advanced weapons to countries like Iraq and Syria.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.970
At this point a full-scale arms race was taking
place in the Middle East, and Saudi Arabia

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.380
was the biggest buyer thanks to the US.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:15.220
"I do not think it contributes towards achieving peace in the Middle East.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.160
And therefore I think this arms sale should be disapproved."

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.240
These sales sparked fierce debates in the
US.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:26.970
Like on June 5, 1986 when President Ronald
Reagan supported the sale of 2,500 missiles

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:27.970
to Saudi Arabia:

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:32.820
"Our proposed arms sales to Saudi Arabia will increase the Saudi's ability to withstand

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.780
the threat from radical Arab states."

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:38.960
Many in Congress were skeptical about
selling more weapons in the name of defense...

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.680
"Over the past 30 years , the US has sold over 50 billion dollars worth

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.780
of military weapons and services  to the Saudis.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.100
More than we've sold to any nation on Earth.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.940
Where are the reciprocal acts of friendship?"

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:56.400
Reagan argued that the arms sales were an
important part of the alliance.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:02.400
"We have had for more than 40 years now, a relationship and an agreement,

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.840
mutual security agreement, with the Saudi Arabians.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.600
And it has been beneficial to both
of us."

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:13.580
He insisted that it was important that the US be the ones to sell weapons to Saudi Arabia…

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.960
"First of all, look, they’re gonna have arms,
whether we do it or not.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:20.810
But when they have them from us, there are
restrictions on their use of them; and that they

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.690
are restricted to using them defensively.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.190
Or then there are things that we will do."

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:31.200
"It is not a very valid argument, but I can use the same argument on drugs out in the street.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.420
If I don’t sell drugs to someone, someone
else will.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:37.650
The question is not whether someone else
will, the question is whether it’s right."

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:41.840
Congress pushed for some changes to the deal before ultimately approving the sale.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.920
In fact, Congress would never fully block a foreign arms sale.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:49.720
Over the next 20 years, the strength of the
US-Saudi alliance would waiver,

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.140
but their reliance on each other never quite
stopped.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.940
The Soviet threat vanished when the country
collapsed in 1991.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:02.500
But Iraq under Saddam Hussein emerged as a
new threat to both Saudi Arabia and the US.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.550
So the Saudis went all out.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:08.880
In 1993, the US and Saudi Arabia agreed on
a record number of arms sales.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.960
But arms sales decreased during the late 1990s
and hit rock-bottom after the 9/11 attacks

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.400
- 15 of the 19 hijackers were Saudi citizens.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:22.300
Two years later, the US launched a war in
Iraq and threw the Middle East into chaos.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:25.170
It turned to Saudi Arabia as a partner and

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.720
arms sales started increasing again.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.360
Over the next decade, the Middle East continued
to fall apart...

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:37.310
And Iran took advantage of the chaos by supporting
militant groups in Lebanon, Syria, and Iraq

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.180
- turning these conflicts into proxy wars.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:46.470
To the US, this is Iran destabilizing the
Middle East, but to the Saudis, this is

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:47.980
Iran closing in on them.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:52.520
So Saudi Arabia started using its weapons - aggressively.

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:02.240
Along with a coalition of allies, Saudi Arabia
intervened in Yemen's civil war in 2015.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.580
The Saudis claimed they wanted to restore
the government, but only made the conflict worse.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:10.740
Iran stepped in to support the rebels, turning Yemen into a proxy war.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.880
The Saudi's aggressive tactics have  created the worst humanitarian

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.780
crisis in the world.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:22.200
Out of nearly 16,000 airstrikes since 2015,
the Saudi-coalition has hit civilian targets

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.860
a third of the time.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:27.470
Most estimates put the civilian death toll well
over 10,000.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:30.160
The UN has found that many of the civilian
attacks were intentional

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.040
and could be considered war crimes.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:37.640
The problem is the US has continued to sell
arms to Saudi Arabia this whole time.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.880
In fact, the Obama Administration approved
the most arms sales to the Saudis in US history.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:47.560
These included not just new weapons, but also
replacements for weapons used or damaged in

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.400
Yemen.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:53.940
Including this bomb: likely sold to Saudi
Arabia in 2015 and dropped on a school bus

00:08:53.959 --> 00:08:54.959
in 2018.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:03.420
"$3 billion dollars, $533 million dollars,
$525 million dollars.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.790
That’s peanuts for you."

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:10.389
While the Trump administration focuses on
the supposed economic benefits of selling weapons, it

00:09:10.389 --> 00:09:13.980
misses the real point:
Decades of arming Saudi Arabia was supposed

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:16.089
to give the US some leverage over it.

00:09:16.089 --> 00:09:18.300
But that's clearly not working.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:22.680
Saudi Arabia’s leader - Crown Prince Mohammed
bin Salman is accused of ordering the brutal

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:25.660
murder of a US-based journalist Jamal Khashoggi.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:29.300
And it’s sparked historic resistance to
the US-Saudi relationship…

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:33.020
"I will not support arms sales until all responsible

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.740
for the death of Mr. Khashoggi have been brought to justice."

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:39.700
And I will no longer support the war in Yemen as constructed."

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:44.380
"The bombing of a school bus full of children and other civilian targets

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:48.480
is not something I want America's fingerprints on."

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.080
So will the US actually stop selling weapons
to Saudi Arabia?

00:09:52.089 --> 00:09:56.529
It’s a difficult question.
The Middle East is more unstable than ever.

00:09:56.529 --> 00:10:00.220
After 75 years, Saudi Arabia and the US still
need each other.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.620
But it’s clearly not a trustworthy alliance
anymore.

